cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Jacquard - Deterministic evidence checking for knowledge synthesis."
message: >-
  If you use Jacquard, please cite it using the metadata in this file.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Riccardo
    family-names: Boero
    email: ribo@nilu.no
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7468-9096"
    affiliation: NILU
repository-code: "https://github.com/open-and-sustainable/jacquard"
url: "https://open-and-sustainable.github.io/jacquard/"
abstract: >-
  Jacquard is open science software being developed for knowledge synthesis,
  with deterministic checks of extracted claims against their source documents.
  Its first-release contract covers schema and claim-rule validation, exact quote location and
  mismatch diagnosis, text and numeric value support, per-claim evidence reports,
  and an audit of filtering by item size. The current implementation provides
  versioned JSON interfaces and interface validation for Go, command-line, and
  C-shared library callers. All acceptance material is synthetic.
keywords:
  - Knowledge synthesis
  - Evidence synthesis
  - Deterministic validation
  - Information extraction
  - Validation
  - Open Source
  - Open Science
